1
00:00:36,850 --> 00:00:43,450
In the lab, many of the chemicals that we come into contact with are potentially hazardous.

2
00:00:43,450 --> 00:00:50,290
Formaldehyde, a common laboratory substance, is no exception, but it is special.

3
00:00:50,290 --> 00:00:54,710
Health problems from mishandling formaldehyde can be extremely serious.

4
00:00:54,710 --> 00:00:59,570
So serious that the Occupational Safety and Health Administration, OSHA, has created a

5
00:00:59,570 --> 00:01:16,820
standard for working safely with materials that contain formaldehyde.

6
00:01:16,820 --> 00:01:22,740
The standard includes a list of health problems associated with overexposure to formaldehyde.

7
00:01:22,740 --> 00:01:27,860
They range from the short-term discomfort of minor burns or of skin irritation to chronic

8
00:01:27,860 --> 00:01:31,780
effects from prolonged periods of overexposure.

9
00:01:31,780 --> 00:01:35,220
Symptoms are easy to recognize.

10
00:01:35,220 --> 00:01:44,500
External contact may cause short-term irritation to the skin, eyes, and mucous membranes.

11
00:01:44,500 --> 00:01:52,100
Inhaling formaldehyde gas or vapors can induce coughing, nausea, violent vomiting, diarrhea,

12
00:01:52,100 --> 00:01:55,060
and laryngitis.

13
00:01:55,060 --> 00:02:00,740
Breathing in extremely high concentrations of formaldehyde can bring on convulsions, a coma,

14
00:02:00,740 --> 00:02:04,400
or even death.

15
00:02:04,400 --> 00:02:09,320
The effects of long-term exposure to high levels of formaldehyde may not appear right

16
00:02:09,320 --> 00:02:13,440
away, but in times, serious problems can develop.

17
00:02:13,440 --> 00:02:18,800
Since formaldehyde is a suspected carcinogen and mutagen, overexposure increases the risk

18
00:02:18,800 --> 00:02:22,720
of developing cancer.

19
00:02:22,720 --> 00:02:24,960
Formaldehyde is also a chronic toxin.

20
00:02:24,960 --> 00:02:31,960
As a result, repeated or prolonged exposure can result in permanent respiratory damage.

21
00:02:31,960 --> 00:02:35,840
Most of these situations can be helped with medical treatment, so if you think you're

22
00:02:35,840 --> 00:02:54,900
developing symptoms of overexposure, report them to your supervisor immediately.

23
00:02:54,940 --> 00:02:59,100
Now that we've looked at the health hazards that are associated with formaldehyde, let's

24
00:02:59,100 --> 00:03:03,340
take a look at how we can protect ourselves when we're working with it.

25
00:03:03,340 --> 00:03:08,920
First, if you're working with high concentrations of formaldehyde or work with it frequently,

26
00:03:08,920 --> 00:03:12,940
you may need to monitor the amount of formaldehyde that you're exposed to.

27
00:03:12,940 --> 00:03:19,220
This is done through testing the air in your immediate work area by taking individual samples.

28
00:03:19,220 --> 00:03:24,460
The test results are then compared to OSHA's permissible exposure limit for formaldehyde,

29
00:03:24,460 --> 00:03:27,180
which is expressed in parts per million.

30
00:03:27,180 --> 00:03:32,420
The current permissible exposure limit is 0.75 parts per million.

31
00:03:32,420 --> 00:03:38,140
This limit is calculated for an 8-hour, time-weighted average of exposure.

32
00:03:38,140 --> 00:03:43,060
If the average level of formaldehyde in the air reaches or exceeds the PEL, you'll need

33
00:03:43,060 --> 00:03:47,900
to take special precautions until the levels are reduced.

34
00:03:47,900 --> 00:03:53,180
For some tasks, looking at an 8-hour average of exposure may mask the presence of temporarily

35
00:03:53,180 --> 00:03:55,580
high levels of formaldehyde.

36
00:03:55,580 --> 00:04:02,160
So to prevent overexposure in these situations, OSHA has established short-term exposure limits,

37
00:04:02,160 --> 00:04:04,260
or STELs.

38
00:04:04,260 --> 00:04:08,260
These limits are based on an exposure period of 15 minutes.

39
00:04:08,260 --> 00:04:16,140
OSHA's short-term exposure limit for formaldehyde exposure is no more than 2 parts per million.

40
00:04:16,140 --> 00:04:20,380
This may seem like a lot of numbers, but exposure limits have been set up for your

41
00:04:20,380 --> 00:04:21,880
protection.

42
00:04:21,880 --> 00:04:24,280
So make sure that you pay attention to them.

43
00:04:24,280 --> 00:04:29,650
If you have any questions, see your supervisor.

44
00:04:29,650 --> 00:04:34,530
The formaldehyde standard also contains a set of training requirements so that everyone who

45
00:04:34,530 --> 00:04:38,970
is using the substance knows how to work with it safely.

46
00:04:38,970 --> 00:04:44,430
Because the adverse health effects of formaldehyde can be so serious, OSHA requires annual training

47
00:04:44,430 --> 00:04:50,170
for all employees who are exposed to levels of one-tenth part per million or higher.

48
00:04:50,170 --> 00:04:55,370
For starters, you need to know where formaldehyde is used in your workplace and how you can limit

49
00:04:55,370 --> 00:04:59,200
hazardous exposure.

50
00:04:59,200 --> 00:05:15,960
Container labeling plays a major role in providing this type of information.

51
00:05:15,960 --> 00:05:20,100
Labels on mixtures and solutions containing more than one-tenth percent formaldehyde

52
00:05:20,100 --> 00:05:25,420
must state specifically that formaldehyde is present and that physical and health hazard

53
00:05:25,420 --> 00:05:32,420
information is available from your employer and the Mixture Safety Data Sheet, the SDS.

54
00:05:32,420 --> 00:05:37,020
This labeling is also required for any material capable of releasing formaldehyde into the

55
00:05:37,020 --> 00:05:42,660
air at concentrations of one-tenth parts per million or higher.

56
00:05:42,660 --> 00:05:46,860
Mixtures and solutions containing more than one-fifth percent formaldehyde and materials

57
00:05:46,860 --> 00:05:51,740
capable of releasing five-tenth parts per million of formaldehyde must be labeled with

58
00:05:51,740 --> 00:05:54,860
the following warnings.

59
00:05:54,860 --> 00:05:59,140
Sensitization of the skin and respiratory system, eye and throat irritation, and acute

60
00:05:59,140 --> 00:06:02,640
toxicity.

61
00:06:02,640 --> 00:06:10,450
These labels must also specifically state that formaldehyde is a potential cancer hazard.

62
00:06:10,450 --> 00:06:15,010
If this information cannot all fit on the container label itself, the label will direct

63
00:06:15,010 --> 00:06:19,890
you to other sources of information such as the SDS.

64
00:06:19,890 --> 00:06:26,170
The SDS will also tell you how to avoid overexposure while you're working with formaldehyde.

65
00:06:26,170 --> 00:06:30,970
In the past, many facilities that used formaldehyde had to purchase it at one-hundred

66
00:06:30,970 --> 00:06:34,090
percent, then dilute it to the strength they needed.

67
00:06:34,090 --> 00:06:40,410
If you were involved in this type of blending process, you should be especially careful.

68
00:06:40,410 --> 00:06:46,610
Nowadays, most formaldehyde comes already diluted in dispenser containers or unit packages,

69
00:06:46,610 --> 00:06:49,810
but you still need to pay attention to how to handle it.

70
00:06:49,810 --> 00:06:54,170
Even in a diluted form, formaldehyde can be hazardous.

71
00:06:54,170 --> 00:06:58,610
There's a reason that OSHA's hazard warning requirements begin at solutions containing

72
00:06:58,610 --> 00:07:14,170
only one-tenth of one percent.

73
00:07:14,170 --> 00:07:18,770
The most basic way of shielding yourself from hazardous levels of exposure to formaldehyde

74
00:07:18,770 --> 00:07:22,850
is through personal protective equipment.

75
00:07:22,850 --> 00:07:25,250
Gloves are a good place to start.

76
00:07:25,250 --> 00:07:30,850
Protective gloves are often designed to be used with specific substances or hazards.

77
00:07:30,850 --> 00:07:34,890
When you're working with formaldehyde, OSHA requires you to choose gloves that are

78
00:07:34,890 --> 00:07:39,930
impervious to solutions of one percent or more.

79
00:07:39,930 --> 00:07:45,170
Things containing more than one percent formaldehyde also require you to wear splash-resistant

80
00:07:45,170 --> 00:07:49,930
goggles that provide complete protection for the eyes.

81
00:07:49,930 --> 00:07:54,530
With some jobs, a face shield may also be required to protect your skin, but don't

82
00:07:54,530 --> 00:07:57,610
consider face shields as a substitute for goggles.

83
00:07:57,610 --> 00:08:02,770
Even with a face shield, goggles are required if there's any danger of formaldehyde reaching

84
00:08:02,770 --> 00:08:05,970
the eye area.

85
00:08:05,970 --> 00:08:10,730
Where formaldehyde gas is present, you may need to use an air-purifying respirator to

86
00:08:10,730 --> 00:08:14,610
protect your nasal passages, throat, and lungs.

87
00:08:14,610 --> 00:08:19,810
You must undergo training and a fit test whenever you're issued a new respirator and at least

88
00:08:19,810 --> 00:08:22,810
once a year thereafter.

89
00:08:22,810 --> 00:08:26,530
When you receive your respirator, you'll also be given the appropriate filter cartridge

90
00:08:26,530 --> 00:08:30,170
for the level of formaldehyde in your work area.

91
00:08:30,170 --> 00:08:35,330
See your supervisor for information about your facility's respiratory protection program.

92
00:08:35,330 --> 00:08:40,290
This will discuss the proper selection, training, and fit testing of respirators, as well as

93
00:08:40,290 --> 00:08:45,520
how often the cartridges will need to be replaced.

94
00:08:45,520 --> 00:08:49,840
In addition to gloves, eyewear, and possibly a respirator, you're also going to need

95
00:08:49,840 --> 00:08:55,600
some type of protective clothing to shield you from splashes when working with formaldehyde.

96
00:08:55,600 --> 00:09:00,680
Lab coats are the most common, but they and any other clothing you wear must be impervious

97
00:09:00,680 --> 00:09:04,600
to water to fully protect you.

98
00:09:04,600 --> 00:09:09,440
If your protective clothing ever becomes contaminated, you should immediately dispose of it in your

99
00:09:09,440 --> 00:09:12,560
facility's authorized disposal area.

100
00:09:12,560 --> 00:09:17,720
Then get a replacement before you start back to work.

101
00:09:17,720 --> 00:09:25,250
Another important part of working safely with formaldehyde is following proper work practices.

102
00:09:25,250 --> 00:09:27,530
The safety data sheet is key.

103
00:09:27,530 --> 00:09:31,770
Be sure to follow all of the recommended handling and storage procedures for the formaldehyde

104
00:09:31,770 --> 00:09:33,930
material that you're using.

105
00:09:33,930 --> 00:09:39,090
It's also extremely important that you follow all of your lab's recommended procedures.

106
00:09:39,090 --> 00:09:43,730
They may require special protective measures, depending on the work you're doing.

107
00:09:43,730 --> 00:09:50,250
Remember, these practices and procedures have been set up for your benefit.

108
00:09:50,250 --> 00:09:54,730
Maintaining proper ventilation in your work area is one of the most important safe work

109
00:09:54,730 --> 00:09:56,730
practices of all.

110
00:09:56,730 --> 00:10:01,530
Be sure to use lab hoods and other ventilation devices to keep any formaldehyde that's

111
00:10:01,530 --> 00:10:05,490
in the air out of your breathing zone.

112
00:10:05,490 --> 00:10:11,450
Not all hoods and air evacuation devices operate the same way, so make sure you know how yours

113
00:10:11,450 --> 00:10:12,450
works.

114
00:10:12,450 --> 00:10:29,140
And be sure to follow all the rules for the safe use of these devices.

115
00:10:29,140 --> 00:10:33,860
Even if you've taken all the recommended precautions, you still need to know what to do in case

116
00:10:33,860 --> 00:10:36,740
an accident with formaldehyde occurs.

117
00:10:36,740 --> 00:10:40,760
No matter how careful we are, things can go wrong.

118
00:10:40,760 --> 00:10:46,400
You need to be prepared so that you can minimize the effects of any mishaps.

119
00:10:46,400 --> 00:10:51,080
To help you with this, your facility has developed a specific plan for dealing with accidents

120
00:10:51,080 --> 00:10:55,840
in your work area, but there are some things that should be done any time an incident

121
00:10:55,840 --> 00:11:00,440
involving formaldehyde occurs.

122
00:11:00,440 --> 00:11:05,400
In the event of a small spill, soak up the liquid with an absorbent material like vermiculite

123
00:11:05,400 --> 00:11:07,440
or a spill pillow.

124
00:11:07,440 --> 00:11:12,720
Place the waste into a properly labeled and sealed container for later disposal.

125
00:11:12,720 --> 00:11:17,680
Do not attempt to handle large spills of formaldehyde.

126
00:11:17,680 --> 00:11:23,280
Formaldehyde is toxic, and the fumes from even a dilute solution can overwhelm you.

127
00:11:23,280 --> 00:11:28,240
Alert other personnel in the area and vacate the laboratory immediately.

128
00:11:28,240 --> 00:11:42,690
Then call for assistance.

129
00:11:42,690 --> 00:11:47,330
If you come into contact with formaldehyde, it's important to act quickly.

130
00:11:47,330 --> 00:11:52,250
For skin contact, immediately remove any contaminated clothing.

131
00:11:52,250 --> 00:11:57,010
Wash the affected area with soap or mild detergent and large quantities of water for at least

132
00:11:57,010 --> 00:12:00,010
15 to 20 minutes.

133
00:12:00,010 --> 00:12:04,210
If the area of contact is large, get to a safety shower.

134
00:12:04,210 --> 00:12:09,010
Remove all your clothing and stay under the water for at least 15 minutes.

135
00:12:09,010 --> 00:12:14,350
Be sure to get medical attention after any contact.

136
00:12:14,350 --> 00:12:20,870
If formaldehyde splashes into your eyes, water is again the first line of defense.

137
00:12:20,870 --> 00:12:25,990
Immediately go to your lab's eyewash station and wash the formaldehyde out of your eyes.

138
00:12:25,990 --> 00:12:29,190
Stay in the water for a minimum of 15 minutes.

139
00:12:29,190 --> 00:12:34,190
Hold your eyes open with your fingers to make sure the water covers the entire area.

140
00:12:34,190 --> 00:12:39,120
Then get medical attention as quickly as possible.

141
00:12:39,120 --> 00:12:45,020
If someone accidentally swallows formaldehyde, immediately provide them with drinking water.

142
00:12:45,020 --> 00:12:50,220
Keep the person warm and calm and get medical attention.

143
00:12:50,220 --> 00:12:55,380
In the event that someone inhales formaldehyde fumes, remove them from the exposure area and

144
00:12:55,380 --> 00:12:57,180
get them to fresh air.

145
00:12:57,180 --> 00:12:59,040
Then call for an ambulance.

146
00:12:59,040 --> 00:13:04,820
Keep the victim warm and calm until medical help arrives.

147
00:13:04,820 --> 00:13:09,580
You need to be careful when responding to any of these accident situations.

148
00:13:09,580 --> 00:13:13,740
Never enter an area that has a high concentration of formaldehyde.

149
00:13:13,740 --> 00:13:19,200
Look for rescuers who have appropriate respiratory protection.

150
00:13:19,200 --> 00:13:23,320
Another way that the formaldehyde standard helps to ensure employee health and safety

151
00:13:23,320 --> 00:13:27,200
is through its medical surveillance plan.

152
00:13:27,200 --> 00:13:32,700
Under the plan, anyone who is adversely affected by exposure to formaldehyde must be given

153
00:13:32,700 --> 00:13:37,360
a temporary work assignment with reduced exposure to the chemical.

154
00:13:37,360 --> 00:13:41,840
After a reasonable amount of time has passed, the facility will then determine whether the

155
00:13:41,840 --> 00:13:46,920
affected employee should return to their old position, remaining the temporary job, or if

156
00:13:46,920 --> 00:13:49,720
other options need to be considered.

157
00:13:49,720 --> 00:14:00,740
If you have any questions about your facility's medical surveillance plan, see your supervisor.

158
00:14:00,740 --> 00:14:05,780
While formaldehyde can be hazardous, we do know how to work with it safely.

159
00:14:05,780 --> 00:14:08,940
Let's review.

160
00:14:08,940 --> 00:14:13,840
Know the hazards that formaldehyde presents.

161
00:14:13,840 --> 00:14:19,850
Be aware of the materials in your work area that contain formaldehyde.

162
00:14:19,850 --> 00:14:25,530
Know what you should do to protect yourself when you work with formaldehyde.

163
00:14:25,530 --> 00:14:31,620
And be prepared to act in case of a spill or other formaldehyde accident.

164
00:14:31,620 --> 00:14:36,660
Knowing the hazards that formaldehyde presents and complying with OSHA's formaldehyde standard

165
00:14:36,660 --> 00:14:42,420
when you use it will make working with formaldehyde easier and safer for everyone.
